<title>CANADA: Canada M1 money supply falls in February.</title>
<headline>Canada M1 money supply falls in February.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian M1 money supply fell by C$17 million to C$68.61 billion in February from C$68.63 billion in January, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					   Feb 97     Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p>M1					  68.61	68.63	58.48</p>
<p>M2					 392.18     394.80     386.93</p>
<p>M3					 499.90     497.80     473.39</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Feb	   Jan</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-19.92	-16.27</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     692.22	685.16</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    105.32	105.23</p>
<p>				    Wk to Mar 19  Chg on wk  Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.480  -0.127     +0.844</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     7.873  -0.979     -0.435</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	461.437  -0.222     +5.633</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 130.600  +1.600    -31.100</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.945  -0.020     +2.125</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
